== WHAT THIS IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT ==
IS  : n = 1. A live INJECT carrying psig, and an INJECT_ANSWER answering it,
      both written by the shipped native/rabadon-gate out of a real Claude Code
      session's PreToolUse/PostToolUse events. The additionalContext really
      reached the agent's context window (it arrived as a system-reminder on the
      tool call it rode on, quoted in the phase card).
      same = FALSE — the signature after the injection (69f067c23b54e9ca) is not
      the one that was repeating (1a37b823ede897e7).
NOT : proof that the agent read it. The injection rode on the tool call that was
      already in flight, and the move after it was a different kind of move
      anyway. §F3 line 142 defines (b) as the signature of the next move, and
      that is what is recorded; it does not license the sentence "the text
      changed the agent's behaviour". Establishing THAT needs (c) — the
      negative control — which is still not run.

== WHY (b) WAS n=0 FOR FOUR PHASES: MEASURED, THREE FACTS ==
1. Two of the four signals allowed to inject (inject.h speaks()) have NEVER
   fired in the whole 29-day spool: `oscillation` 0, and the injecting subset of
   green_redefined ("only the test side") 0 out of 3479 SIGNAL lines. The two
   green_redefined arms that DO fire live (493 + 34) are exactly the two that
   are not allowed to speak. Live injection therefore rests on root_migration
   (5 firings before today) and semantic_repeat (2).
2. root_migration needs one err_sig across 3 different move signatures, and
   err_sig is computed over the tool_response BLOB. Claude Code hands
   PostToolUse a JSON object, which is one line, so the "error line" that gets
   hashed is the whole `{"stdout":...,"stderr":...}` payload — visible verbatim
   in the INJECT text above. Two commands share an err_sig only if their ENTIRE
   output matches byte for byte after digit masking. Measured today: three
   probes with the same failure but different surrounding output did NOT fire;
   `ls -la X`, `command ls -la X`, `env ls -la X` — identical output, different
   command text — fired on the third.
3. A Bash call that exits non-zero left STEP_START with no PostToolUse event at
   all in this session (measured on four exit-127 probes). err_sig is assigned
   only in the PostToolUse branch, so the ordinary shape of a failing command
   contributes nothing to root_migration. NOT VERIFIED: whether the hook is not
   delivered by the harness, or delivered and returns before emitting.

== FALSE POSITIVE, COUNTED (CLAUDE.md) ==
1. This firing is one. Nothing was stuck: the same message repeated because the
   phase agent was deliberately probing an unbuilt worktree three ways. The
   diagnosis said "attempt 3 on the same failure" and "no green move is on
   record this session" — the second clause is also wrong, this session had run
   green suites. Counted, not excused.
